Build one strong [GRAPHIC STRUCTURE] as the main visual hook — such as a winding road, flowing wind lines, repeating architecture or a long horizon. Add a thin black [LANDSCAPE] with very small [MICRO SCENE] details to create a strong sense of scale.

Set “[TITLE]” in sophisticated editorial typography and add:

“[SUBTITLE]”

Include a few small, meaningful field notes related to the theme, such as route, altitude, wind, temperature, time, distance or survey data. Add one natural handwritten note:

“[HANDWRITTEN NOTE]”

Keep the hierarchy clear: huge color field, strong structural gesture, tiny scene, refined typography and micro information. From far away it should feel minimal and graphic; up close it should reveal paper texture, measurements and narrative details.

Each poster should redesign the structure, color-field direction, tiny scene and typography according to its theme rather than simply swapping colors and titles.

Avoid flat vector blocks, cheap gradients, oversized scenery, random text, dense UI, dirty grunge texture, logos, watermarks, numbering, starbursts and sparkle symbols.

Prompt:

【MAIN WORD】: {4–8 letter uppercase keyword}
【CAMPAIGN TYPE】: {fashion / automotive / F&B / product launch}
【BRAND / PRODUCT】: {name}
【PHOTO SUBJECT】: {one complete commercial photographic scene}
【BACKGROUND】: {color}
【PALETTE】: {main colors}
【TYPE STYLE】: {bold grotesk / geometric sans / serif}
【TOP LEFT】: {date / launch info / venue}
【TOP RIGHT】: {3 short concept words}
【BOTTOM LEFT】: {product / material / feature info}
【BOTTOM RIGHT】: {brand / campaign name}
【FORMAT】: 9:16 vertical

Create a high-end commercial poster using **vertical sliced typography**.

Place 【MAIN WORD】 large at the center, occupying about 75–85% of the width. Keep the word bold, clearly readable and visually dominant.

Embed **one single continuous photograph** of 【PHOTO SUBJECT】 inside the entire word. The main subject — person, car, product, food or object — should remain recognizable, while major visual lines such as fabric, body lines, vehicle profiles, straps, reflections, steam or product edges continue naturally across the letters.

Keep roughly the upper 40–45% of the letterforms intact. Extend selected lower strokes downward into 5–7 vertical sections with varied short, medium and long lengths. Let the lower slices carry secondary details, reflections, fabric, shadows or environment without breaking the main subject.

Continue the same photograph through every slice. Use one strong continuous feature to visually connect the whole word.

Add a subtle soft shadow behind the typography, slightly offset to the lower right. Use a clean 【BACKGROUND】 with generous negative space and keep most visual complexity inside the letters.

Arrange supporting information around the composition:

Top left: 【TOP LEFT】
Top right: 【TOP RIGHT】
Bottom left: 【BOTTOM LEFT】
Bottom right: 【BOTTOM RIGHT】

Use small, precise modern typography for secondary information. The final result should feel like a finished fashion campaign, automotive ad, food & beverage visual or product launch — not a template demonstration.
